---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import { ogFor } from '../lib/photos';
import { SITE } from '../config/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '../lib/schema';

const title = 'About AuditYourHome — and how we handle data | AuditYourHome';
const description =
  'Why AuditYourHome exists, how listings are compiled and verified, how program data stays current, and the editorial rules we hold ourselves to.';

const schema = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'About', path: '/about/' },
  ]),
];
---

<Base title={title} description={description} schema={schema} ogImage={ogFor('home-hero')}>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero has-photo">
      <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Why this site exists</h1>
      <p class="lede measure">
        Official tools for finding an energy auditor are bare lists. Rebate programs close with two
        weeks' notice while half the internet keeps advertising them. And the big lead-gen platforms
        sell "energy audit" leads to solar and HVAC reps. Homeowners in Canada and the US deserved a
        better front door — so we built one.
      </p>
      </div>
      <Photo name={'home-hero'} eager />
    </div>

    <div class="measure prose">
      <h2>The rules we operate by</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Only real auditors.</strong> In Canada, every provider we list is an NRCan-licensed
        service organization, whose registered energy advisors deliver the EnerGuide evaluations that
        rebate programs ask for; Ontario's Home Renovation Savings program further limits its assessment
        rebate to seven approved organizations, and every Ontario listing says whether it's one of them.
        In the US, we point you to certified energy auditors (BPI professionals, RESNET HERS raters) and
        the utility and state programs that serve your area. We do not list contractors whose "free
        audit" is a sales pitch, and we say so out loud.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>No pay-to-rank.</strong> Ordering favours transparency (published prices first) and
        community organizations — never payment. If we ever sell placement, it will be labelled as
        such, separately from organic listings.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>How we make money.</strong> In Canada, advisors who opt in pay a referral fee for the
        exclusive homeowner requests we route to them — <a href="/ca/for-professionals/">$40 per lead
        after ten free</a>. It never affects which advisors we list or how they're ordered, each request
        goes to one advisor only, and you can always contact any listed advisor directly instead. In the
        US there are no referral fees: we answer questions by email ourselves and don't pass your details
        to contractors.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Dated claims.</strong> Program facts carry the date we verified them against the
        official page — currently {SITE.dataReviewDate}. We list closed programs on purpose,
        because "still advertising the Greener Homes Grant" is the fastest way to spot a stale
        source.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Estimates labelled as estimates.</strong> The free plan's savings figures are ranges
        based on how similar homes typically perform, and the energy prices, usage benchmarks and
        savings ranges behind them are listed on the planner pages
        (<a href="/ca/plan/#assumptions">Canada</a>, <a href="/us/plan/">US</a>). A home energy audit
        of your actual house replaces them — that's the point.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Corrections are fast.</strong> Listings are compiled from public sources (linked on
        each profile). If something's wrong, email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}> {SITE.contactEmail}</a> and we'll fix or remove it
        promptly. Providers can claim their profiles free.
      </p>
      <h2>What's next</h2>
      <p>
        Online booking, provider-verified profiles, French for Quebec and francophone Ontario, and
        more US metro areas. If you want any of that sooner,
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}> tell us</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose h2 { margin-top: 28px; }
</style>
